{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 80,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As an Australian Canadian"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1440,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Fahrenheit temperature scale has\nalways seemed a bit arbitrary to me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4680,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean why does water\nfreezes at 32 degrees?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7640,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why that integer and what exactly does 0 represent?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11640,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to many sources"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12760,
    "dDurationMs": 2439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Fahrenheit scale was\ndefined by setting 0 degrees"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15200,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "equal to the temperature of\nthe ice salt and water mixture"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17960,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a hundred degrees being\nroughly equal to human body temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21320,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that isn't true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23760,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The real story is much more\ninteresting and scientific."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28600,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "August 14th, 1701 was\nalmost certainly the worst day"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32280,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the life of 15 year-old\nDaniel Gabriel Fahrenheit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35600,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On that day, both of his parents\ndied suddenly from mushroom poisoning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41080,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And he was sent from Poland\nwhere he lived"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43160,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to Amsterdam to become\nan apprentice bookkeeper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46160,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Fahrenheit couldn't\nstand his apprenticeship and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48840,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ran away so many times that his employer\nput out a warrant for his arrest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52760,
    "dDurationMs": 2039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Traveling from city to city around Europe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54800,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he became fascinated with\nscientific instruments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57560,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in particular, thermometers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60040,
    "dDurationMs": 2855,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1708, possibly seeking help\nwith the warrant,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62920,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fahrenheit met with\nthe mayor of Copenhagen,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65160,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who happened to be\nthe famous astronomer Ole Rømer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68760,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rømer is known for observing\nthe eclipses of Jupiter's moons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71600,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and realizing that variations\nin the timing of those eclipses"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74920,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was caused by the time\nit took light to reach Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77665,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, he found a way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78960,
    "dDurationMs": 2196,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to accurately measure\nthe finite speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81600,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, more pertinent to this story,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83240,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 1702, Rømer was housebound\nafter breaking his leg."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86880,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And to pass the time, he devised a\nbrand-new temperature scale"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90240,
    "dDurationMs": 2559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the freezing point of water\nat 7.5 degrees"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92800,
    "dDurationMs": 3615,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and body temperature at 22.5 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96440,
    "dDurationMs": 2799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this might seem odd\nuntil you consider that Rømer wanted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99240,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the boiling point of\nwater to be 60 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101520,
    "dDurationMs": 3055,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As an astronomer, he had\nexperience dividing things by 60."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104600,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you take this scale,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105920,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "divide it in half, in half again\nand in half once more,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109400,
    "dDurationMs": 2719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you find the freezing point of water\none eighth up the scale,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112120,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and human body temperature\nthree eighth up the scale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115360,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So at their meeting in 1708"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117160,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fahrenheit learned of Rømer's temperature\nscale and adopted it as his own,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121440,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "adjusting it slightly because he found it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123400,
    "dDurationMs": 3775,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"inconvenient and inelegant on\naccount of fractional numbers\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127200,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So he scaled them up to 8 and 24."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129880,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is the original Fahrenheit scale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133400,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He produced thermometers\nfor some time using this scale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136880,
    "dDurationMs": 1735,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then at some later point,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138640,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fahrenheit multiplied all numbers\non the scale by 4"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142040,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "setting freezing point to the now-familiar\n32 and body temperature to 96."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146840,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's unclear exactly why he did this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He may just have wanted\nfiner precision in his measurements."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152440,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I think there was a better reason."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see, Fahrenheit was an\nexcellent instrument maker."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158360,
    "dDurationMs": 2375,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "His thermometers agreed\nwith each other precisely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160760,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at a time when that was unheard of."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162840,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He pioneered the use of mercury\nas a measuring liquid,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165720,
    "dDurationMs": 2895,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which has the benefit of a much higher\nboiling point than the alcohol"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168640,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "used in most other\nthermometers at the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170800,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for these accomplishments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172040,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he was inducted into\nthe British Royal Society."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174640,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we know that he read\nthe works of Newton, Boyle, and Hook,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177920,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in which he would have come across the idea"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179680,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that one degree increase in\ntemperature could correspond to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182080,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a specific fractional increase in\nthe volume of the measuring liquid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186200,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And today, a one degree Fahrenheit\nincrease in temperature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188840,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "increases the volume of\nmercury by exactly one part in 10,000."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193480,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is this just a coincidence?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195680,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, we'll probably never know\nfor sure because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198040,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as an instrument maker Fahrenheit\nwas very secretive about his methods."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201400,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I think the data strongly\nsuggest that this was the case."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205280,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, what exactly did zero represent on\nthe scales of Fahrenheit, and Rømer?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210200,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By many accounts, it's the temperature of\nsalt ice and water mixture."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213600,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only problem is there are different\ndescriptions of these mixtures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216480,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And none of them actually produces\nthe temperature they're supposed to."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219880,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More likely, I think they picked the\ncoldest temperature in winter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222800,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "set that as zero"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224240,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and later used ice and brine to\ncalibrate new thermometers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227960,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In his day, the Fahrenheit thermometer\nwas the best you could get."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231760,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now his scale is only\nused regularly in the Cayman Islands,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235240,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bahamas, Belize— oh, and\nthe United States of America."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239800,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So maybe it's time we all\nadopted the global scale of temperature:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244360,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Celsius, which by the way,\nwasn't invented by Celsius at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252920,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey! So that was something\na little bit different."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255720,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video was animated by Marcello Ascani."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259280,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I've got a link to his channel in\nthe description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261600,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, I became really fascinated\nwith temperature scale"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264400,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after I saw the original\nCelsius thermometer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267040,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can see that video here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269360,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this video was supported in part by\nviewers like you on Patreon,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272720,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and by audible.com,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274240,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a leading provider of audiobooks\nwith hundreds of thousands of titles in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277160,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all areas of literature,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278720,
    "dDurationMs": 2175,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "including fiction nonfiction\nand periodicals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280920,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for viewers of this channel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282880,
    "dDurationMs": 1801,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Audible offers a free 30-day trial"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284720,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where you can download\nany book of your choosing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286680,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just go to audible.com/veritasium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288760,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I have a book that\nI would recommend to you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291200,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is called The Structure of Scientific Revolutions\nby Thomas S. Kuhn."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294840,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a classic in the history and\nphilosophy of science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298480,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it'll make you see science\nin a different way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301680,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it shows us that\nscience is not just one process"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304920,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there are actually\nrevolutions that take place"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307640,
    "dDurationMs": 1655,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when big discoveries are made."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309320,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that really changed\nmy thinking about science"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311480,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when I first read this book\nten years ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313360,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can check it out by going to\naudible.com/veritasium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316560,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "downloaded for free and\ntry out the Audible service."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319160,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I want to thank Audible for supporting\nme and I want to thank you for watching."
    } ]
  } ]
}
